{
  "slug": "signal-hunter",
  "name": "Signal Hunter",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Daily AI-powered trend hunter that aggregates content from 15+ sources — HackerNews, GitHub Trending, Reddit, YouTube (with transcripts), X/Twitter, Product Hunt, HuggingFace Papers, Gmail\nnewsletters, and app stores. Detects cross-source trending signals by finding topics appearing in 3+ sources simultaneously, rates them by strength, and generates structured Obsidian notes with\nbusiness ideas (apps, SaaS, BaaS, gaming). Includes daily caching with historical data preservation to reduce API costs. Ships with 5 skills: /digest, /add-source, /test-source, /list-sources, and\n/setup.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **7 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (7): `add-source` (Add a new content source to the daily knowledge builder), `deploy` (Deploy Signal Hunter for automated daily digests — local macOS setup with launchd), `digest` (Run the full daily knowledge digest pipeline — collect from all sources, synthesize trends with scoring and velocity…), `list-sources` (Show all configured sources in the daily knowledge builder grouped by category), `setup` (Set up the Daily Knowledge Builder — install dependencies, configure sources, and create Obsidian vault structure), `test-source` (Test a specific source or category to validate scraping works and output is meaningful), `weekly` (Generate a weekly trend report from the last 7 days of daily digests and cache data)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install signal-hunter@claude-community` from `berkkorkmaz/signal-hunter`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "skill",
